WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is amazing.
So not only the film,

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.736 line:92%
but you have been touring

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.104 size:84% position:42% line:92%
with a Madea stage show

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
as sort of a farewell tour
for you in character.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
130 shows?

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.677 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-130 shows. We're 35 in,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
still sold out, 25,000, 30,000
people a week.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's insane.
-I can't even imagine.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.416 size:78% position:39%
It must be -- I mean,
you've obviously had

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
a relationship with
this character for so long.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't imagine
what that relationship

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.421 line:92%
with the audience is like.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.622 size:78% position:39%
They must be so happy
to be seeing it live.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.358
-Yeah, it's awesome.
I've been doing these live shows

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
for about 20 years now.
And we close --

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.430
Well, the week before we close,
we're here at Radio City,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's going to be pretty,
pretty amazing.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you decided
to wrap it up in Atlanta.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.668
That's going to be the last one?
-Yes, yes.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.304
I wanted to just add at home,
so I can wrap it up at home.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, unless
people are worried,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.907
because I know you've been
saying you might want to

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
retire the character,
but Madea's family funeral,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is not Madea's funeral.
-It's not her funeral.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.147 line:92%
But that old broad is dead, man.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm done. I'm done.
-Really?

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.716 line:92%
-I'm done. I'm done, yeah.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.918
She's been a good character,
she's been a great franchise,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's done really, really well.
But, yeah, it's time.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.124
-And why did you decide to make
her last film at a funeral?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.794
-Well, first of all, I don't
want to be her age playing her,

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I said let's --
time to shut it down.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:06.332
But the funeral thing is --
I've seen so much fun --

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.667 line:92%
and if you ever get a chance,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
please go to
a black person's funeral.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just -- even if you
don't know them,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
just stop by
and sit in the back.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be really,
really long

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're gonna have a really
--

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.479
just write down some notes.
It's hysterical sometimes.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hysterical.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.115 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm happy to hear that.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.483
-Have you ever been to
a black person's funeral?

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.851
-No, but when I go, I'm going to
say you sent me.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:25.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's exactly right.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.120 size:78% position:39%
That's exactly right.
That's exactly right.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.323
-I don't want to just show up.
-Sit there and make notes, yeah.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And -- but, you know,
I heard you say you

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
might be willing to do
a prequel.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.765
We might see young Madea.
-Yes, with a real actress.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Because I'm done.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
No more pantyhose for me,
brother. I'm done.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, with a real actress
playing her

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
from back in the '70s, I think
would be a lot of fun.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I think everybody's fear

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be like how do you
retire a character?

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.175
Are you worried you can't
come up with another one?

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.945
You already have. In this film,
we met a new one, Heathrow.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Heathrow. Her brother.
-Uncle Heathrow, her brother.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you just said

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
you went for it in
a way only you can.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yep, yep, yep.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says he's a war hero.
He lost his legs in the war.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's in a wheelchair,
but the truth is,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.493 line:92%
he got shot by a gangster.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.363
He bought all of his war medals
at Walmart.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.198 line:92%
So he was never in the war.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right, well, I think we
will have a long --

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.902
Hopefully we'll have a long life
with Heathrow, as well.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, he's fun.
-Do people -- I imagine --

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.372 line:92%
because, again, like you said,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
you decided to put
Madea at a funeral.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.675 size:84% position:42%
I imagine your audience
decides all the time

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.145
where they want to see Madea.
Do they pitch ideas to you?

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've heard some crazy ideas.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.782 size:84% position:42%
-Madea goes to England,
Madea goes to Africa,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
Madea goes to Wakanda.
I mean, come on.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.286 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think that's
going to work.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:38.291
-I actually would argue that
it would make a ton of money.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, no.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would check out
Madea goes to Wakanda.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll pass. I'll pass on it.
I'll pass on it.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.866 size:84% position:42%
-You also -- in very --
I mean, I will say this

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.169
really speaks to your range
that you can in the same year

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
play Uncle Heathrow
and Colin Powell in "Vice."

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Isn't that something?
-That is a lot.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are quite an actor.
And you --

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is Adam McKay's film
"Vice."

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:00.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The brilliant Adam McKay.
-Brilliant Adam McKay.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you actually reached out
to Colin Powell.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.618
-Yeah. Before I did it, I wanted
to make sure it was okay.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't want to just, like,
you know --

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're going to play
somebody living,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't want to insult them.
-Sure.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.091 size:81% position:41%
-So if they're dead,
it's like, "Oh, well."

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when they're living,
you want to be like,

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.261 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"Hey, is this okay?"

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was very gracious
and sent me his book to read

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everything,
so it was wonderful.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really exciting.
And you also --

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is really cool.
You're doing --

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:24.804 line:92%
I guess you've already shot it.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're doing a tribute
to Aretha Franklin.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Coming out March 10th, right?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.243
-March 10th. March 10th. Yeah,
I'm hosting, it's really great.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-That's why I couldn't do

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:32.779 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the Oscars, I was busy.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, well I'll get back
to Aretha --

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were at the Oscars.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:39.252
-And you presented, and you made
light of the fact that you --

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.220 line:92%
I think it was Cinematography,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was going to be during
the commercial break.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:45.291
You know, I will say for all the
talk about how the Oscars

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.092 line:92%
had trouble going into it,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it was
a really good night.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a great show
without a host,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I loved it
because it was shorter.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, because you know,

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
it took about 20, 30 minutes
off, not having a host.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.268 size:84% position:42%
I thought it was great.
They did a great job.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.371
-I agree. And I thought there
were some really nice moments.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.839 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But this Aretha thing.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
Aretha was a fan of Madea,
as well?

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.244 line:92%
-Yes. First time she called me,

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was like,
"This Aretha Franklin."

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Oh, my God,
how are you?"

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like,
"I don't want to talk to you.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to talk to Madea."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Well,
you know she's not real."

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.719 size:88% position:44%
She said, "I don't care,
put her on the phone."

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to give her
R-E-S-P-E-C-T.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said --
[ As Madea ] "Hello, hello,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
how are you, Ms. Franklin?
How are you doing?"

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.792
Yeah, yeah, I just went for it.
Just went for it.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was it just wonderful
to pull together --

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, there must have been
so much to pull together

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put together
an Aretha tribute.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well listen, Clive Davis
from Arista

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
and J Records and all that
in the past,

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was the one who pulled it
all together,

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was really fantastic.
-That's great.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:35.908 line:92%
I can't wait to see that.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.011
-The Grammys did it with Clive.
-Okay.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.614
-Or, no, just the Grammys.
I don't want to get in trouble.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.148 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think you covered it.
-Everybody was there.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a black funeral.
We all were there.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
We all were there.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:49.589 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:53.993
-You know, we mentioned Madea
and we mentioned the Oscars.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you did the show...
-Yeah.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.396 line:92%
-...at the Dolby Theatre.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.031 size:78% position:39%
-This was a few weeks
before the Oscars.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.866
-Okay.
-I was playing my farewell tour

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:02.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
there, and that last show
we did,

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.937
we had like 10,000 people
on that Saturday show.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was looking at all these
Oscar people on the wall.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.375 line:92%
Sean Connery with his Oscar

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.444
in these black-and-white images.
They're beautiful.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I went across the street,
bought some fake Oscars,

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
dressed Madea up
in a beautiful gown,

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.585
took a picture, black and white,
and I put it up on the wall.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "By the time
I come to the Oscars,

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.356
somebody is going to see this
and it's going to be gone."

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was still there.
-Yep, there's the photo.

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.727 size:75% position:38%
-It was still there.
It was still there.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Still there.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there's proof
that it's still there.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At the Oscars.
-That's fantastic.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:35.368
-I think the cleaning person
is going to be in trouble.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
How can you clean all these
and not know?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Something is wrong
with this image here."

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.608
-I've got to say, I bet
that for a lot of people,

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
something's very right
about that image

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they have no problem
with that being on the wall.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll take that.
-Hey, man, thank you so much

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being back.
-It's always my pleasure.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.717
-Congratulations.
-Always my pleasure. Thank you.

